Description: storage I/O load balancer for Proxmox VE
 pve-storage-drs equalizes disk I/O load across configurable groups of shared storages
 in a Proxmox VE cluster by live-migrating individual VM disks between the
 storages of a group. It is the storage counterpart to the built-in Dynamic
 Load Balancer, which balances guests across nodes and has no notion of the
 LUNs behind them.
 .
 Placement is solved as a mixed integer linear program over the measured
 per-disk I/O load, subject to a snapshot free-space reserve that must hold
 during a migration and not merely before and after it, and to a payback rule
 that rejects a plan whose own migration cost exceeds the imbalance it removes.
 Load comes from an existing Prometheus; topology and the migrations themselves
 come from the Proxmox VE API.
 .
 The default mode is dry-run: it prints the plan, the arithmetic behind it and
 the API calls it would issue, and changes nothing.
